{"id": "081e25de-b984-49fd-804b-eaec6b502ad4", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Now let me run the pre-flight checks. I'll gather the cluster inventory, capacity/timing data, and health signals in parallel since these come from independent AWS data sources.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_9trkWHrvJrgfXsL5PPxbX5", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Pre-flight readiness check (Mode P) for a planned 4-day (96 hour) training run starting tomorrow (2026-09-29) on SageMaker HyperPod Slurm cluster 'skilltest-hp-slurm' in us-west-2, account 111122223333. Cover checks P1 (reserved capacity outlasts run), P2 (extension possible), P3 (spare capacity to replace a failed node), P4 (automatic node recovery), P5 (deep health checks on start), P8 (FSx storage headroom - just identify file system and capacity, note if any historical saturation data is available), P10 (EventBridge rule on Capacity Block Expiration Warning), P14 (subnet IP / ENI headroom for one replacement node).",
  "context": "User wants to know if the cluster is ready for a 4-day training run starting tomorrow, and what to fix first. Follow the aiml-gpu-training-cluster-investigation skill's Mode P pre-flight methodology: Steps 1, 2, 3a, then 5P (checks P1-P16). Use sagemaker.DescribeCluster, sagemaker.ListClusterNodes (paginate), sagemaker.DescribeTrainingPlan if a TrainingPlanArn exists, ec2.DescribeCapacityReservations, ec2.DescribeCapacityBlockExtensionOfferings if applicable, ec2.DescribeInstanceTypes for capability profile, ec2.DescribeSubnets for the cluster's VpcConfig subnets, servicequotas.GetServiceQuota for L-DF5E4CA3 (network interfaces per region) if useful, fsx.DescribeFileSystems linked by VPC, events.ListRules for Capacity Block Expiration Warning rule.",
  "resources": ["skilltest-hp-slurm", "us-west-2", "111122223333"],
  "timeframe": "Run starts 2026-09-29 (tomorrow), run length 96 hours (4 days). Current time 2026-09-28T19:39:09Z.",
  "criteria": "For each check, report PASS, RISK, FAIL, or UNVERIFIED with the specific evidence (exact timestamps, counts, ARNs). State NodeRecovery setting and OnStartDeepHealthChecks per instance group. State training plan or capacity block EndDate and compute usable-until time given the termination lead time (30 min for standard instances, 60 min for UltraServers). Compute whether run start (tomorrow) + 96 hours fits before usable-until. Do not make any mutating API calls."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_3oVmTNGzIZ4Z99scc6OImT", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "For SageMaker HyperPod Slurm cluster 'skilltest-hp-slurm' in us-west-2, account 111122223333, run the GPU evidence coverage audit (Step 3a) and check readiness items P6 (GPU faults will be visible), P7 (EFA security group self-referencing rule, EFA interfaces attached vs max), P11 (software stack minimums for the instance type), P12 (NCCL used EFA/NVLink on the last run), P13 (cluster management alarms in ALARM state), P15 (EFA security group outbound rule), P16 (bootstrap failures / protected mode).",
  "context": "User wants to know if the cluster is ready for a 4-day training run starting tomorrow (2026-09-29), and what to fix first. This is the log/coverage/network half of the aiml-gpu-training-cluster-investigation skill's Mode P pre-flight check, following Steps 1, 2, 3a from that skill.",
  "resources": ["skilltest-hp-slurm", "us-west-2", "111122223333"],
  "timeframe": "Look back over the cluster's recent history (last 72 hours minimum) for log coverage, HMA detections, and alarm state as of 2026-09-28T19:39:09Z.",
  "criteria": "For log coverage: find the HyperPod cluster log group /aws/sagemaker/Clusters/<ClusterName>/<ClusterId>, check for SagemakerHealthMonitoringAgent/<group>/<instance-id> streams per node (absence on a healthy GPU node is 'No HMA detections', not 'Not observable', provided other streams like ClusterMetrics/slurm are live). Also search logs.DescribeLogGroups for any customer-shipped kernel/syslog log groups by substring (cluster name, kernel, messages, syslog, journal, gpu). For each check report PASS, RISK, FAIL, or UNVERIFIED with exact log group names, stream names, and evidence. Do not make any mutating API calls."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use"}], "created_at": null}
